\begin{mdframed}[style=tipbox]
\noindent\textbf{How these notes work.}
We start from everyday magnets, build the idea of a magnetic field $\vec B$,
then add currents as sources of $B$, then forces on currents and charges, and
finally the d.c.\ motor. Blue boxes = DSE worked examples
(year, correct option, facility~\%). Violet boxes = QB examples.
Orange boxes at the end = practice (answers last). Theory boxes never split
