\section{Formula summary}

\begin{center}
\begin{tabular}{@{}ll@{}}
\toprule
Idea & Formula / rule \\
\midrule
Long straight wire & $B=\dfrac{\mu_0 I}{2\pi r}$ (RH grip) \\
Long solenoid & $B=\mu_0 n I$,\quad $n=N/\ell$ \\
Force on wire & $F=BIL\sin\theta$ (Fleming left hand) \\
Force on charge & $F=|q|vB\sin\theta$,\quad $\vec F=q\vec v\times\vec B$ \\
Parallel wires & same $I$ attract; opposite $I$ repel \\
Permeability & $\mu_0=4\pi\times 10^{-7}\,\mathrm{T\,m\,A^{-1}}$ \\
\bottomrule
\end{tabular}
\end{center}

\begin{mdframed}[style=tipbox]
\noindent\textbf{Before the exam --- five checks.}
(1)~RH grip for $B$ of a wire/solenoid, or Fleming left for force?
(2)~Is the charge positive or negative?
(3)~$\sin\theta$: are $\vec I$ (or $\vec v$) and $\vec B$ perpendicular?
(4)~Dense field lines $\Rightarrow$ force toward the sparse side.
(5)~Motor: what does the commutator reverse, and when is torque zero?
\end{mdframed}

